<title>UK: Agco ready to spend $1.5 billion in Europe.</title>
<headline>Agco ready to spend $1.5 billion in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agco Corp is ready to spend $1.5 billion in European farm equipment acquisitions over the next five years, the Financial Times newspaper reported on Monday. Agco chairman and chief executive, Robert Ratliff told the FT it is &quot;maintaining a dialogue&quot; with a number of companies.</p>
<p>&quot;We have made it clear we are interested in a range of collaborative ventures which might include acquisitions,&quot; Ratliff said. The firms include farm equipment units of Renault, Finland's Valmet, SLH and Landini of Italy, Claas and Fendt of Germany, Dronningsborg of Denmark and Ursus of Poland.</p>
